        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Christening cloak made of cream embroidered cashmere wool, lined with cotton and with two panels of silk at the front edges. It has two capes, both trimmed with eyelet embroidery in a pattern of leaves. The cape collar is five-sided, and set into a high round neck. The cloak and second cape are set onto round yokes underneath the cape collar where they are gathered in small pleats. The cloak opens down the front where it is tied by two pairs of watered silk ribbon. There are two hooks and eyes for fastening in the font, at the top of the neck, and at the yoke."@en ;
